          "content": "You have attempted this same task before and did not succeed. These are the plans you wrote after those attempts.\nTrial #1: New plan: I failed because I entered a repetitive loop between the Utility room, Laundry room, and Workshop without ever checking the remaining unvisited directions (specifically east from the Utility room or west from the Workshop) that could lead to the Solarium and Closet. I also did not explicitly track the set of visited rooms to detect when I was stuck in a cycle. Next time, I will maintain a mental list of visited rooms. Upon entering a room, I will first check if all available directions have been tried; if a direction leads to a previously visited room, I will immediately try the other available direction instead of blindly following the first option. I will only say \"DONE\" when I have visited every unique room in the set.\n\nTrial #2: New plan: I failed because I blindly followed the first available direction without tracking visited rooms, causing me to enter a repetitive loop between the Utility room, Laundry room, and Workshop while missing the Solarium and Closet. Next time, I will maintain a mental set of visited rooms. Upon entering a room, I will check if all available directions have been tried; if a direction leads to a previously visited room, I will immediately try the other available direction instead of blindly following the first option. I will only say \"DONE\" when I have visited every unique room in the set.\n\n\nPlease help me with the following task. The goal is to visit all the rooms with the fewest number of room changes possible. In each room, you need to decide the direction to go in. Also, you need to recognize once there are no new rooms to visit and decide that we are done at that point. Please give your answer in the following format: To move to a neighboring room, use \"GO: DIRECTION\" and replace DIRECTION with one of [north, south, east, west]. To stop the exploration, answer with